<BlogLayout
  title="As-Built Drawings vs. Original Plans: What Is the Difference?"
  description="Original plans show what was designed. As-built drawings show what is really there today. Why the two rarely match, and which one your project needs."
  category="Guide"
  readTime="4 min"
  datePublished="2026-11-17"
  related={[
    { href: '/resources/what-are-as-built-drawings/', label: 'What Are As-Built Drawings? A Plain-English Guide' },
    { href: '/resources/why-every-project-starts-with-as-builts/', label: 'Why Every Building Project Starts With As-Built Drawings' },
    { href: '/quote/', label: 'Get an instant quote' },
  ]}
>
  <p>People often use "blueprints," "plans," and "as-builts" to mean the same thing. They are not the same, and the difference matters when you are about to spend money on a building.</p>

  <p>Here is the simple version:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Original plans</strong> (often called blueprints) show what someone intended to build.</li>
    <li><strong>As-built drawings</strong> show what is actually there today.</li>
  </ul>

