  <h2>Why the two do not match</h2>

  <h3>Changes during construction</h3>

  <p>Buildings are rarely built exactly as drawn. A pipe is in the way, so a wall shifts a few inches. The owner asks for a bigger closet. A window size is out of stock, so a different one goes in. These changes are made on site, and the drawings are usually not updated.</p>

  <h3>Changes over the years</h3>

  <p>After a building is finished, it keeps changing. A kitchen is remodeled. A room is added. A garage becomes a bedroom. New heating and cooling equipment goes in. Each change moves the building a little further from the original plans.</p>

